  ('DIRER_a061_heatsinkSensor', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Abnormal temperature measurements from heatsink sensor', 'Heatsink sensor returns to rational temperature measurements', 'Drive Inverter Warning: Heatsink sensor bad.', 'Unable to monitor heatsink sensor temperature', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4074),
  ('DIRER_a062_systemLimpMode', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU detects abnormal operation in the powertrain system. Alert log signal data provides information on the specific condition(s) detected.', 'A drive cycle is executed and the DI ECU detects that the trigger condition is no longer present.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects a condition that requires it to trigger system limp mode.', 'The performance (torque and power of the drive system) is severely limited.', 'Propulsive power reduced', 'Exiting and re-entering vehicle may restore operation', 'customer;service', 4075),
  ('DIRER_a064_torqueIntervention', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The torque production safety monitor has detected excess torque production and inhibited DIx torque production for the remainder of the drive cycle.', 'Begin a new drive cycle.', 'The torque production safety monitor has detected excess torque production and inhibited Drive Inverter (DIx) torque production for the remainder of the drive cycle.', 'The torque production safety monitor will inhibit torque and excess heat production for the remainder of the drive cycle.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4076),
  ('DIRER_a069_rotorTempLimit', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The rotor''s temperature is too hot, limiting DIx motor torque production. There may be a condition affecting DIx or the motor.', 'The rotor''s temperature returns to a normal range.', 'The rotor''s temperature is too hot, limiting Drive Inverter (DIx) motor torque production.', 'The DIx motor may not produce torque as expected. The Drive Unit may not operate as expected.', 'Approaching high motor temperature', 'Max acceleration reduced', 'customer;service', 4077),
  ('DIRER_a072_gateDriveFaultCounter', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The phase gate drive has detected four fault related signals from the induction motor or ten from the magnet motor. The induction motor or magnet motor may have a condition affecting functionality.', 'Reset phase gate fault counter to zero.', 'The phase gate drive has detected four fault related signals from the induction motor or ten from the magnet motor.', 'The phase gate drive fault counter may block any power stage from enabling. The drive unit may not function as expected.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4078),
  ('DIRER_a073_motorSpeed', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The Drive Unit resolver has detected the motor exceeding typical speed. The rotor or rotor shaft may have a condition affecting functionality.', 'The resolver no longer detects the motor exceeding typical speed.', 'The Drive Unit resolver (motor speed sensor) has detected the motor exceeding typical speed.', 'The motor is exceeding typical speed. The motor and Drive Unit may not function as expected.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4079),
  ('DIRER_a075_motorSpeedMismatch', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The motor speed measured by the Drive Unit resolver does not match the ABS wheel speed sensors. There may be a condition affecting the functionality of the Drive Unit or wiring.', 'The Drive Unit encoder and ABS wheel speed sensors measure the same motor speed.', 'The motor speed measured by the Drive Unit resolver does not match the Anti-lock Braking System (ABS) wheel speed sensors.', 'The Drive Unit may not function as expected, including a reduction in vehicle power. The vehicle''s drive cycle may not function as expected, or at all.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4080),
  ('DIRER_a076_lvSupplyOV', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'LV supply voltage to DI exceeds the set upper voltage limit.', 'The LV supply drops below upper threshold.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects a low voltage (LV) battery overvoltage event.', 'No immediate impact. Could damage drive inverter LV hardware if LV is continuously too high.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4081),
  ('DIRER_a077_lvSupplyUV', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'LV supply voltage to DI (refer to lvSupply) is disconnected or drops below lower voltage threshold', 'LV supply rises back above lower threshold', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects a low voltage (LV) battery power supply undervoltage event.', 'Drive unit enters unit limp mode (see DI_a126_limpMode)', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4082),
  ('DIRER_a078_adcRefLow', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Any ADC channel reference is below the minimum rational value.', 'Clears when all ADC channel references are above minimum rational value for 1 second.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects an analog-to-digital converter (ADC) channel reference below the lower rational bound.', 'The vehicle is blocked from shifting out of Park.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4083),
  ('DIRER_a079_adcRefHigh', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Any ADC channel reference is above the maximum rational value.', 'Clears when all ADC channel references are below the maximum rational value for 1 second.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects an analog-to-digital converter (ADC) channel reference above the upper rational bound.', 'The vehicle is blocked from shifting out of Park.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4084),
  ('DIRER_a086_activeDischargeOn', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Bus voltage is high while active discharge is ON', 'Bus voltage is low or active discharge is off', 'Drive Inverter Warning: Active discharge is on but bus voltage remains high.', 'Potentially exposed high voltage', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4085),
  ('DIRER_a087_gtwMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the GTW, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the GTW.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the gateway (GTW) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the GTW.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4086),
  ('DIRER_a090_pmMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the PM, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the PM.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the pedal monitor (PM) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the PM.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4087),
  ('DIRER_a091_espMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the ESP, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the ESP.', 'The drive interface (DI) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the electronic stability program (ESP, also known as traction control) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the ESP.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4088),
  ('DIRER_a092_bmsMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the BMS, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the BMS.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the high voltage (HV) battery management system (BMS) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the BMS.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4089),
  ('DIRER_a096_memoryError', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The bootloader cyclic redundancy check (CRC) or application CRC is not expected, or the RAM constants do not match with initialization segment in flash.', 'Clears automatically 5 seconds after being set.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects a memory check error.', 'The DI processor may reset, and other functionality may be impacted due to memory corruption.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4090),
  ('DIRER_a097_eepromError', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'There are read/write issues to EEPROM.', 'Clears when the vehicle is in Drive or Reverse if triggered on a primary unit, or when the unit is enabled if triggered on a secondary unit.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects an electrically erasable programmable read-only memory (EEPROM) read/write access error. Check for other alerts that may be set as a result.', 'The DI is not able to store any record in EEPROM where the error is located, which impacts functionality on the next boot up.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4091),
  ('DIRER_a098_intTimeTooLong', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DIx has detected a DIx thread executing later than expected. The DIx CPU may be diverting resources towards other tasks.', 'This alert is for logging purposes and clears automatically.', 'The Drive Inverter (DIx) has detected a DIx thread executing later than expected. The DIx CPU may be diverting resources towards other tasks.', 'This alert is primarily informational and is used for logging purposes. No expected impact on vehicle functionality.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4092),
  ('DIRER_a103_lowFlow', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Insufficient cooling to the drive inverter is detected', 'Cooling is sufficient and a drive cycle is executed', 'Drive Inverter Warning: Low flow rate of fluid.', 'Drive unit enters unit limp mode (see DI_a126_limpMode)', 'Rear right motor power may be limited', 'OK to drive - Schedule service', 'customer;service-fix', 4093),
  ('DIRER_a107_fpgaError', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'DIx has detected an error communicating with FPGA. There may be a condition affecting the DIx control board functionality.', 'The DIx no longer detects an error communicating with FPGA. May require DIx be replaced.', 'The Drive Inverter (DIx) has detected an error communicating with the Field Programmable Gate Array (FPGA).', 'The DIx Gate Drive Unit may not be able to receive data from the Pedal Monitor. The vehicle''s drive cycle may not function as expected.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4094),
  ('DIRER_a108_stateTrans', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The Drive Unit is not able to transition to Drive state. There may be a condition preventing the Drive Unit from transitioning states.', 'Beginning a new drive cycle may clear the alert.', 'The Drive Unit is not able to transition to Drive state. There may be a condition preventing the Drive Unit from transitioning states.', 'The Drive Unit may not function as expected, including a reduction in vehicle power. The vehicle''s drive cycle may not function as expected, or at all.', 'PULL OVER SAFELY', 'Exiting and re-entering vehicle may restore operation', 'customer;service', 4095),
  ('DIRER_a110_brakeMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the EPB, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the EPB.', 'The drive interface (DI) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the electronic parking brake (EPB) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the EPB.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4096),
  ('DIRER_a111_badPhaseSensorCalib', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DIx EEPROM has reported phase sensor calibration is outside valid range.', 'The DIx EEPROM no longer reports phase sensor calibration being outside valid range.', 'The Drive Inverter (DIx) Electrically Erasable Programmable Read-Only Memory (EEPROM) has reported phase sensor calibration is outside valid range.', 'This alert is primarily for logging purposes and appears in conjunction with other alerts.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4097),
  ('DIRER_a112_noPhaseCurrent', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DIx ECU detects no phase current. The phase lugs, stator, rotor, or DIx may have a condition affecting functionality.', 'The DIx ECU detects an expected quantity of phase current.', 'The Drive Inverter (DIx) Electronic Control Unit (ECU) detects no phase current.', 'Without phase current, DIx cannot produce motor torque to rotate the wheels. The vehicle''s drive cycle may not function as expected, or at all.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4098),
  ('DIRER_a113_noFuncHeatsinkSensor', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The three DIx heat sink sensors are not functioning. The DIx heat sink sensors may have a condition affecting functionality.', 'The DIx detects normal output from the three heat sink sensors.', 'The three Drive Inverter (DIx) heat sink sensors are not functioning. The DIx heat sink sensors monitor temperature in the motor and fluid port.', 'Since it cannot detect temperature as expected, DIx may limit power output to an operational level. Drive Unit performance may be impacted.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4099),
  ('DIRER_a116_highSpeedWearCounter', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Number of qualified high speed events above allowed threshold', 'Non-clearable', 'Drive Inverter Warning: High Speed Wear Counter Exceeded.', 'Silent alert to track mechanical wear', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4100),
  ('DIRER_a117_diMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DIx node is MIA on CAN for one or more messages. The DIx node or DIx may have a condition affecting functionality.', 'The DIx node resumes communication with CAN.', 'The Drive Inverter (DIx) node is Missing in Action (MIA) on Controller Area Network (CAN) for one or more messages.', 'DIx may not be able to communicate with the High Voltage Processor (HVP).', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4101),
  ('DIRER_a119_hvpMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the HVP, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the HVP.', 'The drive interface (DI) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the high voltage processor (HVP) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the HVP, and active discharge may turn on.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4102),
  ('DIRER_a120_hvlinkMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Any received HVLINK frame is MIA', 'All consumed HVLINK CAN frames received', 'Drive Inverter Warning: HVLINK CAN node MIA.', 'Active discharge may turn ON', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4103),
  ('DIRER_a121_motorControlRegulation', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Motor regulation fails to meet command inputs', 'Reason for trigger is not present', 'Drive Inverter Warning: Motor control is out of regulation.', 'Drive unit enters unit limp mode (see DI_a126_limpMode)', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4104),
  ('DIRER_a123_lossMotorControl', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Motors are not responding to DI commands', 'Motors respond to DI commands', 'Drive Inverter Warning: Loss of motor control.', 'Unable to produce torque/power from drive unit', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4105),
  ('DIRER_a126_limpMode', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Abnormal condition detected within drive unit subsystem. Look at limpReason in alert for exact trigger.', 'Reason for trigger is not present and drive cycle is executed', 'Drive Inverter Warning: Unit limp mode triggered.', 'Drive system performance severely reduced (torque/power limited)', 'Rear right motor power reduced', 'Exiting and re-entering vehicle may restore operation', 'customer;service', 4106),
  ('DIRER_a127_gracefulPowerOff', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Drive Unit GPO has been triggered. The Drive Unit will lose current input from the HV battery.', 'GPO is no longer in effect.', 'Drive Unit Graceful Power Off (GPO) has been triggered. The Drive Unit will lose current input from the High Voltage (HV) battery.', 'The Drive Unit will ramp down all torque production. The Drive Unit may not function as expected.', 'Power Reduced', 'PULL OVER SAFELY', 'customer;service', 4107),
  ('DIRER_a133_capacitorOT', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'DIx has detected the capacitor is over temperature. The pack contactors may have a condition affecting functionality.', 'The DIx no longer detects the capacitor being over temperature.', 'The Drive Inverter (DIx) has detected the capacitor is over temperature.', 'The flow of current between the capacitors and DIx may not function as expected.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4108),
  ('DIRER_a134_wheelSpeedIrrational', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU receives irrational or no data from the WSS.', 'The DI ECU receives expected/rational data from the WSS.', 'The drive interface (DI) electronic control unit (ECU) receives irrational or missing data from a wheel speed sensor (WSS).', 'This alert is primarily informational. If it persists, traction control may become unavailable.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4109),
  ('DIRER_a136_spiError', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'DIx has detected an error communicating with SPI, which monitors the pedal monitor. There may be a condition affecting SPI.', 'The DIx no longer detects an error communicating with SPI. May require DIx be replaced.', 'The Drive Inverter (DIx) has detected an error communicating with the Serial Peripheral Interface (SPI), which monitors the pedal monitor.', 'DIx may not be able to receive data from the Pedal Monitor. The vehicle''s drive cycle may not function as expected.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4110),
  ('DIRER_a140_eggright3MIA', 'Cybertruck', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the EGGRIGHT3, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the EGGRIGHT3.', 'The drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the Etherloop Generalized Gateway Right (EGGRIGHT3) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the EGGRIGHT3.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4111),
  ('DIRER_a144_configMismatch', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Set if any of the checked gateway config is not as expected.', 'Clears when all of the checked gateway configurations are as expected.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects a Gateway configuration mismatch with the application currently running on the DI.', 'The vehicle enters system limp mode and is unable to enter Drive.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4112),
  ('DIRER_a145_vcleftMIA', 'Cybertruck', 'One or more of the expected messages from the VCLEFT ECU is not received.', 'The vehicle controller starts receiving the expected messages from the VCLEFT ECU.', 'One or more of the messages the vehicle controller receives periodically from the Left Vehicle Controller (VCLEFT) Electronic Control Unit (ECU) is not received, indicating the VCLEFT ECU may be unavailable (MIA).', 'The vehicle controller is unable to monitor the state of the VCLEFT ECU.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4113),
  ('DIRER_a147_highTorqueWearLimit', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'DIx has detected a quantity of torque production that indicates Drive Unit wear.', 'This alert is primarily intended for logging purposes and clears automatically.', 'The Drive Inverter (DIx) has detected a quantity of torque production that indicates Drive Unit wear.', 'The Drive Unit may have wear resulting from torque production. The vehicle may enter launch mode torque.', 'Powertrain requires service - OK to drive', 'Avoid hard acceleration - Schedule service', 'customer;service', 4114),
  ('DIRER_a149_oilPumpFailure', 'Cybertruck', 'Loss of communication or power to oil pump, persistent oil pump motor stall occurred, or persistent condition affecting oil pump functionality detected', 'Clears at the start of a drive cycle, if set condition is not present anymore', 'Drive Inverter Warning: Oil pump failure.', 'Initiates reduced drive unit performance and a speed limit on the vehicle, due to reduced gear lubrication and motor cooling', 'Powertrain requires service', 'Vehicle speed and power may be limited', 'customer;service-fix', 4115),
  ('DIRER_a149_oilPumpScavengeFail', 'Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Loss of communication or power to oil pump, or persistent oil pump motor stall or fault occurred', 'Clears at the start of a drive cycle, if set condition is not present anymore', 'Drive Inverter Warning: Oil pump failure.', 'Initiates reduced drive unit performance and a speed limit on the vehicle, due to reduced gear lubrication and motor cooling', 'OK to drive - Powertrain requires service', 'Vehicle speed and power may be limited', 'customer;service-fix', 4116),
  ('DIRER_a150_busVD', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The HV bus has measured a voltage drop in the HV battery pack. DIx may not operate as expected.', 'The HV bus measures normal voltage in the HV battery pack.', 'The High Voltage (HV) bus has measured a voltage drop in the HV battery pack. The Drive Inverter (DIx) may not operate as expected.', 'DIx may not operate as expected. Drive torque may be restricted.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4117),
  ('DIRER_a152_linError', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DIx ECU has detected an error communicating with LIN. The DIx LIN node(s) or LIN signal-carrying wire may have a condition affecting functionality.', 'The DIx ECU no longer experiences errors communicating with the LIN.', 'The Drive Inverter (DIx) Electronic Control Unit (ECU) has detected an error communicating with the Local Interconnect Network (LIN).', 'DIx and the oil pump communicate through LIN. DIx may not communicate with the oil pump as expected.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4118),
  ('DIRER_a154_resolver', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The Drive Unit resolver is not operating as expected. The resolver may have a condition affecting functionality.', 'The resolver begins functioning as expected. Review the logs to crack alert.', 'The Drive Unit resolver (motor speed sensor) is not operating as expected. The resolver may have a condition affecting functionality.', 'The resolver is not operating as expected. The DIx invertor control board may be unable to correctly detect the angle and speed of the rotor.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4119),
  ('DIRER_a155_vcfrontMIA', 'Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the VCFRONT, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the VCFRONT.', 'The drive interface (DI) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the front vehicle controller (VCFRONT) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the VCFRONT.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4120),
  ('DIRER_a155_vcsuperMIA', 'Cybertruck', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the VCSUPER, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the VCSUPER.', 'The drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the Supermanifold Vehicle Controller (VCSUPER) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the VCSUPER.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4121),
  ('DIRER_a157_rcmMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the RCM, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the RCM.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the restraints control module (RCM) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the RCM.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4122),
  ('DIRER_a158_ibstMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the IBST, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the IBST.', 'The drive interface (DI) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the iBooster (IBST, or brake assist) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the IBST.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4123),
  ('DIRER_a160_busVoltageAnomaly', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The HV bus has measured a voltage anomaly in the HV battery pack. DIx may not operate as expected.', 'The HV bus measures normal voltage in the HV battery pack.', 'The High Voltage (HV) bus has detected a voltage anomaly in the HV battery pack. The Drive Inverter (DIx) may not operate as expected.', 'DIx may not operate as expected. Drive torque may be restricted.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4124),
  ('DIRER_a161_epas3pMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU is not receiving the expected CAN communication from the EPAS3, and considers it irrational or MIA.', 'The DI ECU receives the required CAN messages from the EPAS3.', 'The drive interface (DI) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the electronic power assisted steering, gen 3 (EPAS3) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the EPAS3.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4125),
  ('DIRER_a172_statorOilTempOT', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Stator temperature exceeds upper temperature threshold for stator thermistor oil protection.', 'Stator temperature drops below upper temperature threshold for stator thermistor oil protection.', 'The drive inverter detects that the stator is over temperature for oil protection.', 'Drive unit enters unit limp mode and it can be damaged if temperature is continuously too high.', 'Motor overheating', 'PULL OVER IMMEDIATELY', 'customer;service', 4126),
  ('DIRER_a174_unitMayNotRestart', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Inverter detects a shorted switch', 'Does not clear', 'Drive Inverter Warning: Unit may not allow drive on the next drive cycle due to HW damage.', 'Inverter may not allow drive on next drive cycle', 'Vehicle may not restart', 'Service is required', 'service', 4127),
  ('DIRER_a202_excessHeatUnavailable', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects a condition that prevents the drive unit(s) from generating excess heat. Alert log signal data provides information on the specific condition(s) detected.', 'The DI ECU detects that the condition clears.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects a condition that prevents the drive unit(s) from generating excess heat.', 'The drive unit(s) cannot produce excess heat when requested.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4128),
  ('DIRER_a234_pcsMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU does not receive the expected CAN messages from the PCS.', 'The DI ECU receives the expected can messages from the PCS.', 'The drive interface (DI) or drive inverter (DIx) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the power conversion system (PCS) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'The DI ECU is unable to monitor the state of the PCS.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4129),
  ('DIRER_a236_tasMIA', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI ECU does not receive the expected CAN messages from TAS.', 'The DI ECU receives the expected CAN messages from TAS.', 'The drive interface (DI) electronic control unit (ECU) detects that the Tesla air suspension (TAS) controller area network (CAN) node is missing (MIA).', 'TAS may be unavailable.', 'Adaptive ride control may be unavailable', 'OK to drive - Proceed with caution', 'customer;service-fix', 4130),
  ('DIRER_a240_clearFusesRoutine', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The clear fuses routine was attempted. The alert log signals provide more information on what the routine did and its results.', 'This alert does not clear until the affected drive unit motor is serviced or the Drive Inverter ECU is reset.', 'This alert indicates the fuse clearing routine was attempted.', 'The motor is permanently disabled.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4131),
  ('DIRER_a242_spinDownLearning', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Drive unit rotor offset, rotor flux, or resolver error learning routine is in progress.', 'Spindown learning calibration routine is completed, or the routine is aborted.', 'Drive unit spindown learning calibration routine is in progress.', 'Drive unit torque is limited and pending spindown sequence.', 'Spindown learning in progress', 'Power reduced', 'service', 4132),
  ('DIRER_a244_mechSafeStateApplied', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Software detects a shorted semiconductor switch. The alert log signals provide detailed trigger algorithm info.', 'Clears when low voltage (LV) power is removed from drive unit or a non-drive/drive cycle occurs', 'Alert for software trigger of mechanical safe state two-phase disconnect device.', 'The motor is permanently disabled.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4133),
  ('DIRER_a246_recoveryAtSpeedError', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'The DI detects the at-speed recovery mechanism encounters an error affecting its functionality. Alert log signal data provides information on the specific condition(s) detected.', 'Clears automatically.', 'The Drive Interface (DI) detects the at-speed recovery mechanism encountered an error.', 'The vehicle may lose propulsion.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 4134),
  ('DIRER_a247_rotorOffsetError', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Rotor offset mean estimator is above minimum rationality threshold at very low absolute torque outputs', 'Rotor offset mean estimator falls below minimum rationality threshold', 'The Drive Interface (DI) detects the rotor is irrationally offset.', 'Diagnostic alert data only, may indicate reduction in torque or excess heat accuracy', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 4135),
  ('DIRER_a251_oilPumpService', 'Cybertruck;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+', 'Adverse oil pressure detected or DC current sensor rationality degraded, see reason payload', 'Adverse pressure condition or sensor condition has been cleared', 'Drive Inverter Warning: Oil pump service.', 'Drive Unit thermal estimation and limits are conservative, potential torque limiting with aggressive driving, recommend inspecting drive unit oil level and oil pump', 'Gearbox fluid service required', 'Schedule service', 'customer;service-fix', 4136),
