  ('ESP_a118_hfcActive', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'HFC is activated because all of the following conditions have been met: (1) the master cylinder pressure exceeds a certain pressure; (2) the Anti-lock Braking System (ABS) is not active; (3) the vehicle does not decelerate in time.', 'HFC is no longer active.', 'The Electronic Stability Program (ESP) detects that the one or more of the brakes are faded, causing Hydraulic Fade Compensation (HFC) to be activated.', 'Braking performance may be reduced due to faded brakes. The ESP pump may be activated to increase the brake pressure.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7841),
  ('ESP_a119_hbbActive', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'The HBB is activated because the brake pressure is too low for a given brake pedal stroke.', 'The HBB is no longer active.', 'The Electronic Stability Program (ESP) detects that the brake pressure is too low for the given brake pedal stroke, causing the Hydraulic Brake Boost (HBB) to be activated.', 'Braking performance may be reduced. The ESP pump may be activated to increase the brake pressure.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7842),
  ('ESP_a120_rmiActive', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'RMI is active.', 'RMI is no longer active.', 'Roll Over Mitigation (RMI) is active. The Electronic Stability Program (ESP) may activate the brakes to help stabilize the vehicle.', 'The ESP may attempt to prevent the vehicle from rolling over by engaging the brakes.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7843),
  ('ESP_a121_regenTcActive', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'Regenerative Traction Control is active.', 'Regenerative Traction Control is no longer active.', 'Regenerative Traction Control is active. The Electronic Stability Program (ESP) may try to prevent wheel slips under regenerative braking.', 'No expected impact on vehicle functionality. The vehicle should be driven with caution due to the road conditions.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7844),
  ('ESP_a124_ebrSkidActive', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'The ESP detects the vehicle is skidding with locked wheels.', 'The ESP detects the vehicle is no longer skidding with locked wheels.', 'The Electronic Stability Program (ESP) detects that the vehicle is skidding while the wheels are locked.', 'No expected impact on vehicle functionality. The vehicle should be driven with caution due to the road conditions.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7845),
  ('ESP_a134_steeringAngleInvalid', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'EPAS3P_internalSASQF is received as invalid', 'Verify EPAS is awake, in good state, and there is traffic present on the bus. Review EPAS/DI alerts for other indicators of failure', 'Invalid Data Received From Steering Angle Sensor Module: Invalid Signal Status.', 'May fault VDC/TC, ABS performance degradation', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7846),
  ('ESP_a135_steeringAngleNoCenter', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'EPAS3P_internalSAS fails plausibility check for center position', 'Verify EPAS is awake, in good state, and there is traffic present on the bus. Review EPAS/DI alerts for other indicators of failure', 'Invalid Data Received From Steering Angle Sensor Module: Invalid Signal Status.', 'May fault VDC/TC, ABS performance degradation', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7847),
  ('ESP_a136_steeringAngleFrozen', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'EPAS3P_internalSAS is frozen on CAN', 'Verify EPAS is awake, in good state, and there is traffic present on the bus. Review EPAS/DI alerts for other indicators of failure', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor: Constant signal detected.', 'May fault VDC/TC, ABS performance degradation', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7848),
  ('ESP_a137_steeringOffsetTooLarge', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'Steering offset received from EPAS outside of threshold', 'Check steering alignment and steering offset. Review EPAS/DI alerts for other indicators of failure.', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor: Adjustment not possible (Offset too large).', 'May fault VDC/TC, ABS performance degradation', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7849),
  ('ESP_a138_steeringAngleImplaus', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'The monitoring checks for a physically plausible steering angle signal and consists of following parts:- Sas range monitoringReceived raw sensor hardware value is higher than the maximum, physical steering wheel turn from zero-position to lock in the vehicle (LwAnschlMax) + an additional robustness tolerance value (typical 90 deg)- Sas gradient monitoringIf the signal gradient (steering angle velocity) from one 20 ms-cycle to another is higher than 40 deg for 2 SAS Messages (60 deg for more than 2 SAS messages or no SAS message counter) or - change of this gradient (steering angle acceleration) is higher than 30 deg a failure will be set.- Sas plausibility versus yaw rateThe difference between measured steering angle signal and model value calculated from yaw rate signal is evaluated for fault detection. Dependent on the driving conditions failures in size of (10 + 60 [m/s] / velocity [m/s]) deg at steering angle are recognized through three possible recognition paths evaluating stable driving conditions. This is to prevent a fault recognition due to unstable driving.When the difference is caused by a fault of the steering angle sensor a steering sensor angle fault will be entered. The sensor - yaw rate sensor(YRS) or steering angle sensor(SAS) - showing the largest deviation to the reference yaw rate is marked as faulty.', 'Verify EPAS is awake, in good state, and there is traffic present on the bus. Review EPAS/DI alerts for other indicators of failure', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor: Plausibility fault.', 'May fault VDC/TC, ABS performance degradation', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7850),
  ('ESP_a139_steeringAngleWrongSign', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'This monitoring detects a wrong sign of steering angle signal. The yaw rate calculated from steering angle and the yaw rate calculated from the wheel speed sensors are compared. If the measured yaw rate fits to the model yaw rate positive integrals (IVzLwVA and IVzLwHA) are calculated but if the negative values fits the integrals will become negative. A fault is determined if the integral value is negative and forward driving is recognized. This fault will cause a release test in the following ignition cycle to assure that the sensor is build in correctly. This fault can also be caused by swapped WSS lines at one axle. It requires a release check in the following ignition cycle to prevent system release when the fault is still present. The conditions for release is positive integrals (IVzLwVA and IVzLwHA) > +180 deg.', 'Verify EPAS is awake, in good state, and there is traffic present on the bus. Review EPAS/DI alerts for other indicators of failure', 'Steering Wheel Position Sensor: Plausibility fault.', 'May fault VDC/TC, ABS performance degradation', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7851),
  ('ESP_a144_yawMaxLatency', 'Cybertruck;Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'Yawrate signal received from RCM exceeds message latency specification', 'Inertial messages are present/valid on the bus. Review RCM/DI alerts for other indicators of failure', 'Invalid Data Received From Air Bag Control Module : Invalid Yaw Signal Status.', 'May fault VDC/TC, ABS performance degradation', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 7852),
