  ('VCLEFT_a254_seatUncalLift', 'Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'Motor calibrated is 0', 'The motor is calibrated', 'The lift motor is uncalibrated.', 'Position recall unavailable', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 16616),
  ('VCLEFT_a255_LVOverchargeInstc', 'Cybertruck', 'Over a single charge cycle, the LV battery has recharged by more than 5Ah compared to the power initially discharged.', 'The LV battery is no longer recharging by more than 5Ah compared to the amount discharged.', 'After a single discharge and recharge cycle, the low voltage (LV) battery has been overcharged by more than 5 Amp hours (Ah) compared to initial charge level. If this continues, it may indicate a condition affecting LV battery performance that makes replacement necessary. May also indicate aftermarket device(s) installed on the vehicle, whose current draw interferes with LV battery management.', '10 independent instances of this alert indicate a chronic overcharge condition that may require LV battery replacement to resolve, and at least  one other alert should be present to indicate that condition.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 16617),
  ('VCLEFT_a257_leftHeadlampNotAimed', 'Cybertruck', 'A replacement left vehicle controller (VCLEFT) has been installed.', 'The headlights are aimed using the user interface (UI) or the headlight aiming ODIN routine is run for the left headlight.', 'The vehicle controller detects that the left headlight has not been aimed or requires re-aiming.', 'The headlights may not properly illuminate the area in front of the vehicle or may dazzle oncoming drivers.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 16618),
  ('VCLEFT_a259_LVVoltageDropOnHighLoadCurrent', 'Cybertruck', 'An instant resistance check of the LV battery connections to the vehicle controller does not succeed (does not return a healthy result). Alert log signal data should provide more information on specifics, including load current, LV battery temperature, and any detected voltage dip.', 'Clears automatically.', 'The vehicle controller detects the low voltage (LV) battery voltage is lower than expected during a precharge event. When this occurs too many times, separate alerts will also be present to indicate precharging the high voltage (HV) bus may not succeed and the LV battery may need replacement.', 'The LV battery may be unable to support vehicle electrical systems, including precharging the high voltage (HV) bus.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 16619),
  ('VCLEFT_a260_deadLVBattery', 'Cybertruck', 'The vehicle controller detects LV battery voltage or LV battery Amp hour (Ah) budget are below their limits for 5 seconds.', 'The vehicle controller detects LV battery voltage and the Amp hour (Ah) budget are no longer below their limits.', 'The vehicle controller detects the the low voltage (LV) battery may be overdischarged and no longer functional. This may indicate the LV battery has been damaged due to deep discharge, or it may indicate the LV battery voltage has dropped below the minimum limit for maintaining functionality.', 'The LV battery may be unable to hold adequate electrical charge to remain functional. Replacement may be necessary, with a separate alert present to indicate that condition if applicable.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service-fix', 16620),
  ('VCLEFT_a261_emergencyLatchRelRear', 'Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'Door opened without electronic release', 'Door is closed', 'The mechanical release was used to open the door.', 'Posible trim damage', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 16621),
  ('VCLEFT_a261_winchModeWithoutSteering', 'Cybertruck', 'Winch Mode is enabled, but the EPB did not receive the expected messages from the steering system.', 'Winch Mode is disabled.', 'The Electronic Parking Brake (EPB) enabled Winch Mode but did not receive the expected messages from the steering system.', 'Steering performance may be reduced or steering may be unavailable until Winch Mode is disabled.', 'Steering is unavailable', 'Proceed with caution', 'customer;service', 16622),
  ('VCLEFT_a267_seatTrackHCEncStlDbg', 'Model 3 2017-2023;Model 3 2024+;Model S 2021+;Model X 2021+;Model Y;Model Y 2025+', 'Current draw exceeded 70% of the stall limit, and the encoder did not move for 100ms.', 'The motor is not in a movement state. It may also be in a movement state, but has not detected a high current motor stall.', 'The seat track motor encoder has unexpectedly stalled.', 'The seat track motor encoder may increment incorrectly if an obstruction is encountered.', 'Not Available', 'Not Available', 'service', 16623),
